// The interactive client's state, the overlay stack and the key table.
//
// This is the bottom layer of the client. `GIT_client.m31` used to be one
// 3000-line module with one `State` type; m31 allows a method only in the
// module that declares its type and refuses import cycles, so the client is
// now a tower of layers, each one an embedding of the one below it:
//
//   GIT_ui_core     Core            state, overlay stack, key table, command log
//   GIT_ui_outline  OutlineLayer    outline cursor, stage / unstage / discard
//   GIT_ui_diff     DiffLayer       the hunk-level diff view
//   GIT_ui_commit   CommitLayer     the commit overlay, amend
//   GIT_ui_branch   BranchLayer     the branch overlay, check out, new branch
//   GIT_ui_remote   RemoteLayer     the push and pull overlays
//   GIT_client      State           the whole client: draw, key dispatch, $EDITOR
//
// Embedding promotes fields and methods, and every layer holds the SAME `Core`
// (a struct is a reference), so a method in `DiffLayer` reads `message` or
// calls `reload()` exactly as it did when it was a method of one big `State`,
// and an overlay that holds a layer reference can drive everything below it.
// `GIT_ui_help`, `GIT_ui_log`, `GIT_ui_search` and `GIT_ui_picker` are
// overlays that need only `Core`.
//
// --- overlays ---------------------------------------------------------------
//
// An `Overlay` is a modal thing drawn over the document: it takes every key
// while it is on top of `Core.overlays`, draws itself, and says which keys it
// answers to so the footer can show them. There used to be five booleans
// (`is_commit_open` and friends) and an if-chain of five handlers; now
// opening an overlay is `push_overlay`, closing it is `pop_overlay`, and
// stacking them (the help overlay over the commit overlay) just works.
//
// --- the key table ----------------------------------------------------------
//
// `key_table()` is the one place a key is bound. Dispatch (`lookup`), the
// footer (`hints_for`) and the `?` help overlay (`bindings_in`) all read it,
// so the footer cannot advertise a key that does nothing, and a new binding
// shows up in the help overlay without anyone remembering to add it there.
//
// --- the command log --------------------------------------------------------
//
// Every operation that WRITES to the repository calls `log_command` with one
// line ("stage a.txt", "commit 1a2b3c4", "update-ref refs/heads/x old..new").
// The `@` overlay shows the ring buffer.

